  { number := 238, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 239, text := "" },
  { number := 240, text := "Work that claims this specification conforms if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 241, text := "" },
  { number := 242, text := "1. Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) is treated as the ideal, and the PDOSS test is the public domain dedication of software that is open (Clause 3.4, Clause 3.5, and Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 243, text := "2. Unlicense remains the license; the most important Surmount work in this repository is dedicated to the public domain under the Unlicense; companion Lean treats an Unlicense dedication as having no remaining copyright in the model and as meeting the PDOSS test (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 244, text := "3. MIT as used by the Lean 4 agent skill pack does not meet a public domain dedication test and does not meet the PDOSS test; Apache 2.0 as used by the `btc-verified` pin does not meet a public domain dedication test and does not meet the PDOSS test; a mash that claims MIT meets PDOSS is `False` (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 245, text := "4. A grant that keeps copyright is treated as still leaving a copyright holder, and remaining copyright is treated as still letting a later contract take the work (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 246, text := "5. Ideas are treated as not scarce; two people can hold the same idea at once; generosity of ideas is the default this repository chooses (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 247, text := "6. Numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree are released under the Unlicense except where residual names a different license; the Lean 4 agent skill pack remains MIT; the `btc-verified` pin remains Apache 2.0; essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are not Unlicense (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 248, text := "7. Refusing a tool the author cannot improve is treated as RSI process residual and is not treated as a claim that every product is Unlicense (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 249, text := "8. Numbered markdown is the contract humans read; the specification is encoded in Lean as declarations of what must be true; proofs live in separate Lean modules; a mash that hides the split is treated as `False`; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 250, text := "9. Formal Vibefication citations keep the canonical Proof of Keags URL; a numbered specification that names Keagan or Proof of Keags also contains the host `proofofkeags.com`; theorems cover exactly what they state (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 251, text := "10. beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, Continuous Integration, Lean Machine, and Majestic Memex are treated as ongoing and not ready for use, and are not described as never started or as ready (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 252, text := "11. fargo, SSSP, and Carbonado remain unspecified; Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; number 0009 is this specification and is not assigned to fargo or Carbonado; a numbered Vocabulary file does not exist; the Unlicense numbered markdown file for specification 0009 does not exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept (Clause 4.10)." },
  { number := 253, text := "12. The named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate for this repository (Clause 4.11)." },
  { number := 254, text := "" },
