  { number := 302, text := "### 0.1.0 - 20260901" },
  { number := 303, text := "" },
  { number := 304, text := "Current version line is 0.1.0 by operator order. Number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS). The file name is `0009_PDOSS.md`. Unlicense remains the license. Defines the PDOSS test. Records that Unlicense meets that test. Records that MIT as used by the Lean 4 agent skill pack and Apache 2.0 as used by the `btc-verified` pin do not meet a public domain dedication test. Records that a mash that claims MIT meets PDOSS is `False`. Residual records that other public domain instruments (for example CC0) are not pinned here. Changelog history records that a 1.0.0 line existed for Unlicense as numbered specification 0009, and that number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then Unlicense, and is now PDOSS." },
  { number := 305, text := "" },
  { number := 306, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260826" },
  { number := 307, text := "" },
  { number := 308, text := "First publication of Unlicense as numbered specification 0009. The operator assigned 0009 to fill the gap after Vocabulary was folded into CATE. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then withdrawn; it was then Unlicense by operator order. A numbered Vocabulary file remains forbidden. Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). This document does not steal 0011 for fargo. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. Records that a grant that keeps copyright still lets a later contract take the work. Requires the most important Surmount work in this repository (numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree) to be dedicated to the public domain under the Unlicense so it stays the common heritage of anyone who seeks it, outside a later private claim. Records that ideas are not scarce and that two people can hold the same idea at once. Requires authors to release numbered specifications and the Lean in this tree under the Unlicense except where residual names a different license. Records that the Lean 4 agent skill pack remains MIT and that essays by Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) are not Unlicense. Records that refusing a tool the author cannot improve is RSI process residual and is not a claim that every product is Unlicense. Records Formal Vibefication as the split that encodes this specification in Lean and keeps proofs in separate modules, with canonical Proof of Keags URLs and back linking. Treats a mash of spec encodings and their proofs that hides the split as nonconforming. Requires residual honesty that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are ongoing and not ready for use." },
  { number := 309, text := "" },
  { number := 310, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: CATE is specification 0005; RSI is specification 0006; Formal Vibefication is specification 0008; Surmount Systems is specification 0010; this specification is number 0009; the word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`); a numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist; number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`); this document does not steal 0011 for fargo; number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept; fargo has no assigned specification number; SSSP is not specified; Carbonado has no assigned number; Lean Machine is specified as `0013_Lean_Machine.md`; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` whose physical lines match that markdown, with proofs in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`, checked by `line_encodings_check`; honesty notes for Proof of Keags copies live at `ref/philosophy/proofofkeags/SOURCE.md`; this document does not claim that a conforming Surmount product exists." },
